prompt:
The team needs to send a notification by email or SMS depending on the user's preference -- two fixed cases, with no roadmap item for a third channel. A developer proposes a classpath-scanning plugin framework:

```java
public class NotificationPluginLoader {
    public List<NotificationChannel> loadPlugins() {
        // scans the classpath via reflection for classes annotated
        // with @NotificationPlugin, instantiates them reflectively,
        // and registers them in a dynamic rule engine
    }
}
```

so that "new channels can be dropped in without touching existing code." A teammate instead proposes:

```java
public void notify(User user, String message) {
    switch (user.getPreferredChannel()) {
        case EMAIL -> emailSender.send(user, message);
        case SMS -> smsSender.send(user, message);
    }
}
```

Which approach better fits the KISS principle for the problem as it actually stands today?
